    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** (66.42) and **Lawrence Butler** (65.46) anchor our lineup as the clear top performers. **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Alcantara, where his ability to capitalize on the right-handed platoon advantage and his prime spot in the #2 hole makes him our most efficient asset. Simultaneously, **Lawrence Butler** is in a prime position to deliver; his efficiency score is buoyed by a +13% platoon adjustment against Burrows, making him a high-leverage start to hunt for both HR and counting stats. **Luis Arraez** also presents a strong profile at 63.51; despite a minor downgrade for the wind blowing in, his matchup against Taillon remains favorable enough to keep him locked into the #3 spot as a vital AVG stabilizer.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was limiting **Gleyber Torres** (49.11) to the bench. He hovered near the threshold for a marginal start, but the current efficiency of **Matt Chapman** (58.74) and **Bryson Stott** (57.88) provides a better projected outcome, even with **Bryson Stott** facing a stiff challenge against the tough Gilbert. While **Gleyber Torres** offers value, the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon dynamics favoring our starters against their respective right-handed opponents today. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** start closely; facing deGrom (3.13 xERA) is a significant risk factor that suppressed his score to 53.23. While we never sit our stars, the -19% penalty for facing an elite arm limits our expectations for massive production today. Elsewhere, **Taylor Ward** and **Drew Gilbert** are facing Gausman and Taillon respectively; while their scores are lower, their presence in the lineup is essential to maintain our volume. With **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** still sidelined on the IL, we must rely on our depth pieces like **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jung Hoo Lee** to fill the gaps and keep our SB production from bottoming out, despite the headwinds of difficult matchups for some of our bottom-of-the-order hitters.",
